# Prisma Best Practices

## Schema Conventions
- Model names: **PascalCase**, singular (`User`, not `Users`)
- Field names: **camelCase**
- Use `@id`, `@unique`, `@relation` properly
- Always include `createdAt` and `updatedAt` (use `@updatedAt`)
- Use soft delete with `deletedAt DateTime?` when needed
- Index foreign keys and frequently queried fields

```prisma
model User {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  email     String   @unique
  name      String
  posts     Post[]
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([email])
  @@map("users")
}
```

## Query Patterns

### Select only needed fields
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  select: { id: true, email: true, name: true },
});

// ❌ BAD - fetches everything
const users = await prisma.user.findMany();
```

### Pagination
```typescript
const PAGE_SIZE = 20;

const [items, total] = await Promise.all([
  prisma.post.findMany({
    skip: (page - 1) * PAGE_SIZE,
    take: PAGE_SIZE,
    orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
  }),
  prisma.post.count(),
]);
```

### Avoid N+1
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Use include/select
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  include: { author: { select: { id: true, name: true } } },
});

// ❌ BAD: N+1 queries
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany();
for (const post of posts) {
  post.author = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id: post.authorId } });
}
```

### Transactions
```typescript
// ✅ Use transactions for multi-step operations
await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  const user = await tx.user.create({ data: userData });
  await tx.profile.create({ data: { userId: user.id, ...profileData } });
  return user;
});
```

## Migrations
```bash
# Create migration
pnpm --filter backend prisma migrate dev --name add_user_table

# Apply to production
pnpm --filter backend prisma migrate deploy

# Reset DB (dev only)
pnpm --filter backend prisma migrate reset
```

## Type Safety
```typescript
// ✅ Use generated types
import { Prisma, User } from '@prisma/client';
import { UserRepository } from './user.repository';

async create(data: Prisma.UserCreateInput): Promise<User> { ... }

// ✅ Use Prisma.UserWhereInput for complex filters
```

## Soft Delete
```prisma
model Post {
  id        String    @id @default(cuid())
  deletedAt DateTime?
  // ...
}
```

```typescript
// Always filter by deletedAt: null
prisma.post.findMany({ where: { deletedAt: null } });

// Use Prisma middleware for global filter
```
